WEBVTT

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:12.710
<i>After Gramps died,
sound stopped speaking to me.</i>

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.210
<i>I needed something.</i>

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.120
<i>I searched...</i>

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.770
<i>and searched...</i>

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.880
Music Prep Room

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.880
Okay!

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.880
Let's get this Shamisen
Appreciation Club meeting started!

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.130
Right!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.500
And if you're wondering, I rented these
shamisens from a Japanese instrument shop!

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.520
<i>How did it turn out like this?</i>

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.810
Oh! I also asked them to repair
Seiryuu-sama's instrument!

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.190
"Sama"?

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.590
It's starting to feel like
a real club now, isn't it?

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.880
Well, starting with form
is always important.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.490
But what are we supposed to do now?

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:50.860
It's not like there's an inter-high school
competition to aim for.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.520
You'd think that, wouldn't you?

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.030
But there's this!

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:55.520
Sponsored by Umemaru,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.160
the Tsugaru Shamisen Koshien:
The Matsugorou Cup!

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.060
Isn't it amazing?

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.420
It's perfect timing! Almost like
they knew we were forming a club!

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.760
<i>You wanna know the secret behind my beauty?</i>

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.790
Umemaru's that cosmetics company
that's making waves right now, isn't it?

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.170
<i>This is it: Umemaru moisturizing gel cream.</i>

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.420
Sawamura-kun, is something wrong?

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.300
It... It's nothing.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.600
But it says here that groups need
to have five or more members.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:20.670
What?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:21.770
Oh, then we can't do it.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.610
You'd think that, wouldn't you?

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.760
But we have a new member!

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:27.930
What?

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.770
Thanks for having me!

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.940
You...

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.940
My mother is a shamisen instructor, you see.

00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.070
So I've played for my dad's
performances and stuff like that.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:38.740
But...

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:43.240
Now I want to put the sound front
and center, and see what it's like to cut loose.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.240
I can do that with a futozao, right?

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.590
Rai-chan, you're so cruel!

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.840
You promised you'd make us lots of animals!

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.290
Oh, you silly gooses!
I'm not quitting the Handicrafts Club!

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.450
You mean it?

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.680
So now we've got our members
and we've settled on a goal.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.470
Sure I do.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.980
Time to start practicing so we can win!

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.040
Win?

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:26.500
Those Snow

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:26.500
White Notes

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.020
<i>I'm not interested in
other people's performances.</i>

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.610
<i>And my goal is Gramps' sound.</i>

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:47.050
Sawamura-kun!

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.560
U-Um... I couldn't say it earlier, but...

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:55.300
Do you think you could teach everyone
the shamisen, Sawamura-kun?

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.000
Huh?

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.150
Me?

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.180
Sawamura

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:03.180
Episode 5
Playing Together

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.180
Hello, Sawamura speaking.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.540
Oh, it's you, Setsu? What's up?

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.540
Huh?

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:11.390
You're going to be teaching
shamisen to novices?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.010
That's gonna be rough.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:25.350
Okay! I can play "Sakura" now!

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.820
I've got it down perfectly, too.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.560
Dear, oh dear. Please don't be
satisfied just yet.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.340
All I'll say is this: the piece for the Tsugaru
Shamisen Koshien is "Jongara Shinbushi."

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.190
The shamisen is my friend. I am not afraid!

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:38.830
Huh?

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:43.290
Hey. Did you really ask Sawamura to coach us?

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.010
Oh, uh, yeah...

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.380
But I think maybe he doesn't
want to teach people like us.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.050
You're late, Sawamura!

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.970
Come on. Let's play the entry piece.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:57.480
We're not playing "Shinbushi" yet.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:58.770
Huh?

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.530
The first thing you need
them all to learn is...

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:03.530
"Roku-dan."

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.530
We'll start with that.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.990
"Roku-dan"?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.640
Well, seems appropriate, doesn't it?

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.530
"Roku-dan" serves as a base for "Jongara."

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:15.620
It's almost like a primer
piece for Tsugaru shamisen.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.960
Oh! If we're doing "Roku-dan"...

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:21.640
When I rented a shamisen, it came with
some sheet music that included that song.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:22.520
See?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:24.880
Tsugaru
Shamisen

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.420
Huh?

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.520
Could it be...

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.130
...he doesn't know...

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.870
...how to read music?

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.190
B-But it's not like we'll have
sheet music for the performance!

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.600
It's better if Sawamura-kun
just teaches us without it.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.110
Music Prep Room

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:42.110
Posture. Don't look down. Keep your head up.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:43.870
Look at my hand.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.110
String one.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.680
Kaito, your string is flat.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:54.620
He's dropping honorifics with me?

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.610
Next, string two.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.120
Back position transitioning to front.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:05:59.250
Go.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.420
One thing does worry me.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:17.850
You've only ever played with
people who know how to play.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:20.650
Make sure you don't get angry with
people who don't know anything yet.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.650
<i>Everyone's like this in the beginning.</i>

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.710
In the beginning...

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.250
The beginning...

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.100
Wrong string again.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.060
The begin

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:48.170
Hey, am I in tune?

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.130
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.300
Oh gosh...

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.880
I can't seem to get it.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.990
Do you think this shamisen is broken?

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.490
Of course it isn't.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.110
W-Well, anyway, we still have
time before the competition.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.360
We're just getting started.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.490
It's impossible.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.660
Hey!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.160
You could at least give us
a little encouragement.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.330
I'm done.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:24.880
I don't know how much you can improve
if you can't even produce a decent sound.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.080
If you want to do it, go ahead.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.550
But I have no intention of
lowering myself to your level.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.770
Who do you think you are?! This is
my first time touching a shamisen!

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:40.560
We're desperate here! Put yourself
in our shoes before mouthing off!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.620
Kai-chan!

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.620
<i>I'm not angry with any of them.</i>

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.070
<i>I'm angry at myself.</i>

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:49.390
<i>It's me I'm irritated with.</i>

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.850
<i>But what am I upset about?</i>

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.790
I'm staying out of this.

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:57.840
There doesn't seem to be any hope.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:00.360
What a predicament.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.240
What took you so long?

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.620
Umeko?!

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.700
Is seeing Mama after so long
getting you all emotional?

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:27.150
Looks like you've been practicing.
Don't slack off before the big competition.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.480
Oh, that's right! What do you think you're doing?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.030
You even slapped Gramps' name on it!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.720
It's insane, ya know.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.460
Putting together a competition
just swallows up money.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.500
Wait, surely you didn't make
me go to high school for <i>this</i>?

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.040
Of course not.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:43.810
But the timing really is perfect, isn't it?

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:47.260
The inaugural winner of a competition
bearing Matsugorou's name...

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.870
It's the perfect place to show
what you can <i>really</i> do.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.080
I'm only competing in the group division.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:59.290
Though, I'm not really sure what's
going to happen with the group...

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.840
You'd better be messing with me!

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.180
I'm not messing around!

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.340
I made this competition!

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.280
You <i>have</i> to enter the individual division!

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.390
I knew it! This whole thing was
set up to drag me into the spotlight!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:13.700
D-Dad!

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.620
I'm gonna go check on Setsu-san!

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:19.230
Just leave them. Families have their own circumstances sometimes.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.500
They say the more you fight,
the closer you are, right?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.580
Y-You think that's what it is?

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.840
Matsugorou was amazing!

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.720
He was truly incredible!

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:34.970
But no one knows that!

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.340
I am Matsugoro's daughter!

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.540
And, Setsu, you have talent.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.340
I won't let your talent smolder
away in obscurity like his did!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.560
I am your mother!

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:51.300
I'll leave it at that for today.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:54.160
Think about entering the
individual competition.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:59.100
The shamisen world... No, the whole music
industry is watching this competition.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.640
Kids who have distinguished
themselves in junior categories

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:05.200
or have played alongside adults
will be coming from all over the nation.

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:09.120
And so will the guy who placed second in
the Hirosaki Tournament, ahead of Wakana:

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.210
Tanuma Souichi.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.800
At just eighteen years old,

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.840
Tanuma Souichi gave
a staggering performance.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.830
Tanuma Souichi...

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.560
Tanuma

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:28.060
Someone's holding a Tsugaru
Shamisen Koshien in Tokyo!

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:29.580
We're in the middle of a lesson.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.820
It's possible Sawamura Setsu will enter it.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.660
See? I mean, it's called the "Matsugorou Cup"!

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.700
I already heard about that
from my teacher at school.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.270
Seems like it'll be stupid amounts of fun.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:48.460
<i>Yes. You are as beautiful as ever today...</i>

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:50.330
<i>...my Kiyora 2.</i>

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:57.130
<i>I was sure I'd already tucked away</i>

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.500
<i>what I felt back then.</i>

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.920
<i>I was starving at the time.</i>

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:08.270
<i>It simply isn't possible to
awaken those feelings once more.</i>

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:15.040
<i>"Kamiki Seiryuu-sama..."</i>

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.690
<i>"Please listen to the worries
I have as an instructor."</i>

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:22.060
<i>"The truth is, everyone's struggling to get
along in the Shamisen Appreciation Club."</i>

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:25.200
<i>"At this rate, I don't know if we'll
even be able to enter the competition."</i>

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:27.070
<i>Competition?</i>

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.720
<i>"Sawamura Setsu-kun has been teaching the
others, but maybe it was too much for him."</i>

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:36.450
<i>"This is Sawamura-kun playing 'Shinbushi.'"</i>

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.680
<i>"But I don't know if this is right or not."</i>

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.740
<i>"He can't read music, you see."</i>

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:52.290
<i>It's sharp and harsh... Wild and fierce...</i>

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.320
<i>His fingering and bachi
are all over the place!</i>

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.440
<i>I don't understand.</i>

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:57.940
<i>I don't understand!</i>

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:02.550
<i>What would happen if Sawamura
Setsu unleashed his true sound?</i>

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:04.440
<i>I just don't know!</i>

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:08.870
<i>I don't understand.</i>

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.670
Did you hear? They say Setsu-kun's dad...

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:15.030
No way!

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.420
<i>My sound...</i>

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:17.710
<i>Whose sound is it?</i>

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.970
You inherited the living
spirit of his sound, didn't you?

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.100
I am your mother!

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:28.970
Why aren't you gonna
be in the competition?

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:34.930
Oh, how unusual.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.030
<i>I don't understand.</i>

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:45.710
<i>I don't understand...</i>

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:50.620
<i>I don't understand!</i>

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:56.570
<i>I want a sound that isn't bound by anything!</i>

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:06.550
So Sei ShЕЌnagon lifted the bamboo curtains
and showed Empress Teishi the scenery.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.330
U-Um, Sawamura-kun...

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.910
Do you have some time right now?

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:38.270
Um, well, the thing is...

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.760
I'm sorry about the other day.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:40.760
What?

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.190
I ruined the mood.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:44.640
Oh, n-not at all! It was us who...

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:46.510
We're not very good.

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:49.520
I'm not surprised you got fed up
with us, Sawamura-kun.

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:54.520
I loved my Gramps' sound.
I wanted to be just like him.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:00.940
It was fine when I had him there
as my goal, but now that he's gone,

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.150
it's become a shackle.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:06.150
A shackle? Your grandfather, you mean?

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.540
No one's interested in me.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.720
It's the thing that's supporting me
they want to hear: Gramps' sound.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.490
You are <i>you</i>, Sawamura-kun!

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:20.330
Sawamura-kun, you have your own sound!

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.700
Don't you remember what my grandma said?

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:25.050
You have a gentleness that heals.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.010
And you didn't just heal my grandma...

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.720
You healed me, too.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:33.530
I was able to help my
grandma hear that song again.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:35.690
I accomplished my goal.

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.940
But I didn't want that to be the end
of my Tsugaru shamisen journey.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:43.030
And it's all because I was so moved
by your sound, Sawamura-kun.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.500
Even though I know it's impossible,

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:48.440
I wanted to try to get
just a little closer to it.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.370
That's why I want to
perform in the competition.

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.000
I want all of us to work hard together.

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:04.800
Oh, you two! There you are.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.640
Koyabu-sensei?

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:10.030
You weren't in the classroom,
so I've been looking for you.

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:12.310
See, the thing is, I've got big news!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:19.190
Ta-da! Kamiki Seiryuu-san has
come to see how you're all doing.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:20.430
Eek! In the flesh?

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:21.690
Why? But how?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.760
Oh, my! He's so handsome!

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:24.200
Huh?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:25.320
What?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:28.800
I told him you were all working
toward entering a competition.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.710
So he offered to listen to you
play and give you all advice!

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:35.660
<i>I admit, it's a poor excuse.</i>

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:38.540
Excuse me. We're really grateful and all,

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:42.560
but other than Sawamura, no one here
can play the set piece, "Shinbushi."

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.160
Do you plan on matching
Sawamura's style for it?

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.660
They aren't matching mine.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.510
Mine is all over the place.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:50.890
Really?

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.130
Well then, let me hear it.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.590
You'll listen to mine, and then what?

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.590
I'll give you advice.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:15:59.820
<i>I'll listen, and then what?</i>

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:03.840
I've heard your sound twice now,

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.890
but I don't think you showed
your true ability either time.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:10.700
<i>Have I come this far... out of curiosity?</i>

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.730
<i>Or a sense of restless disquiet?</i>

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.610
In that case, thanks in advance for the advice.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:29.510
<i>He's not going to slack off again, is he?</i>

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.630
<i>I-I need to record this!</i>

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.810
<i>Hm? Is this the same piece he played before?</i>

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.790
<i>It's a completely different piece now!</i>

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.570
<i>Where he adds in the phrases...</i>

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:01.850
<i>It's not just the number of times...
The tone is different, too.</i>

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:04.880
<i>You wouldn't think it was
the same person playing.</i>

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.040
<i>It's softer than before.</i>

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.350
<i>I see.</i>

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.840
<i>You really are mercurial, aren't you?</i>

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:21.390
<i>But...</i>

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:23.910
<i>you still have a way to go.</i>

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:51.920
<i>Even though there are days when a musician
cannot play a song they have mastered well,</i>

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.600
<i>they will still play efficiently.</i>

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:59.280
<i>But with him, everything changes
depending on how he feels.</i>

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:02.760
<i>It's because you insist on
having it all your own way.</i>

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.050
<i>But I won't let you do as you like.</i>

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:46.040
<i>Sawamura-kun's quick,
delicate, skipping sounds...</i>

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:49.880
<i>are riding on top of Seiryuu-san's
smooth, sprawling sounds...</i>

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:52.610
<i>What is this?</i>

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.150
<i>Is this the birth of something new?</i>

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.120
<i>A chemical reaction?</i>

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:07.540
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.660
<i>It's like his sound is supporting me.</i>

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:17.450
<i>The sound just naturally leaps and dances.</i>

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:20.730
<i>It dances...</i>

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:24.270
<i>...and dances...</i>

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:27.280
<i>...and dances!</i>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.570
<i>This is...</i>

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:45.820
<i>...playing together!</i>

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:11.690
We didn't end up getting any advice.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.440
Asking for advice with our skills is
just rude, so it's better this way.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.950
But we'll never have such
an opportunity, you know?

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:21.700
Oh, really now. He gave us
something even better than advice.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:22.620
He did?

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.300
You didn't notice?

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:28.230
That man played the phrases in
"Shinbushi" in the most basic way possible.

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:29.580
The most basic way?

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.510
That's right. Which means...

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:33.950
What's wrong, Yui-chan?

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:38.880
K-Kamiki Seiryuu and Sawamura's
ensemble performance...

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:42.420
...falls just within the
tournament's time limits.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.950
What?

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.920
You see? I knew it.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:51.490
S-So... if we learn the basic version,
we'll be able to play like Seiryuu-san!

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:53.870
That's what it would mean, yes.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:55.460
What a guy!

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.700
He was able to match Sawamura perfectly
their first time playing together.

00:20:58.920 --> 00:20:59.880
You're wrong.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.200
He didn't match his playing to me.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.700
He made me match him.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:10.760
He locked away Kamiki Seiryuu's phrasing
and challenged me with just the basics.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.250
So what did you think?

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.580
How did it feel getting pulled along
by your partner's performance?

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.450
Must've been frustrating, right?

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.060
Not really.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.080
Oh! Where are you going?

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:23.940
Bathroom.

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:28.320
Dear, oh dear. He ran away.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.350
It really must've upset him, huh?

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:34.150
Wait. Did he just skip?

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.450
<i>The feeling of being pulled along.</i>

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:41.930
<i>It's not frustrating, exactly...</i>

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:46.570
<i>But it did irk me a little.
And it was also sort of fun...</i>

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:48.870
<i>Oh!</i>

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.770
This isn't barley tea! It's noodle broth!

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.080
It's so salty...

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:59.380
<i>This is how I felt when
Gramps played pranks on us.</i>

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.620
<i>This is the first time
I've felt this good in a long time.</i>

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:10.460
Dragging Setsu-kun out of
his shell is going to be tough.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:13.470
Forget "dragging" him out.

00:22:13.470 --> 00:22:15.970
I ended up going out to see him myself.

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:17.790
It is what it is.

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:20.360
I just couldn't hold back those \emotions.

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:45.210
Oh! They were together for the first time!

00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:49.130
Games and shamisen are a lot alike.

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:52.280
If we're going to do this, let's <i>really</i> do it!

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:54.010
Okay. Once more from the top.
